      {
        "id": 97593,
        "name": "jffdougan",
        "username": "jffdougan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/{size}/1882_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-29T02:57:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"EdgeDS\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n EdgeDS:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Greywind wrote:</b><br><blockquote>...and it was <strong>AWESOME</strong>!\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;Yyyyyyup. &nbsp;While I enjoyed Ghost Story and Cold Days, I felt they didn't measure up well to Changes. &nbsp;Skin Game definitely did, IMO.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>See, I'm strange on this front – my favorites are still absolutely Summer Knight and Small Favor. What I enjoyed most about this one was that it feels more like one of the pre-Changes books.</p>",
